      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your observation reflects an ongoing debate in art history between the \"democratization\" of art through political engagement and the necessity of formalist aesthetic experience. While more politically driven works can make art more socially relevant and accessible to a broader audience, some critics argue they risk prioritizing didactic messaging over the intentional craft and visual innovation that traditionally defined modernist value. Ultimately, the impact on contemporary art's overall value is complex because it has expanded the definition of what constitutes significant art, even if it has arguably shifted the center of gravity away from purely aesthetic contemplation toward sociopolitical commentary.",
