    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, i hear you, but isn't there a clear distinction between \"complexity\" and just being heavy-handed? it feels like a lot of these \"contemporary\" pieces aren't even trying to be art anymore, they're just trying to virtue signal or push a specific agenda. if a piece only works if you already agree with the politics behind it, hasn't it fundamentally failed as a piece of art?",
